WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.860
Avengers: Endgame clocked in at a whopping
three hours, making it the longest Marvel

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:09.490
movie to date, but there are still scenes
that were cut from the final film that we

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:10.540
never got to see!

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:14.940
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing all the deleted and

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.590
fake scenes from Endgame.

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:21.029
A new round of my Marvel giveaway is running,
so subscribe and leave a comment about the

00:00:21.029 --> 00:00:22.679
movie for a chance to win.

00:00:22.679 --> 00:00:25.860
Of course, we'll be discussing spoilers, so
take care if you haven't seen the film yet.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:26.970
And there's timestamps for each main section
in the video description below.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:31.050
If you were devastated by Black Widow's heroic
sacrifice in Endgame, then you'll be shocked

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:34.400
to know that a stack of Natasha scenes were
cut from the final film.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.289
First is a deleted scene of Nat at target
practice where she's keeping her shooting

00:00:38.289 --> 00:00:39.730
skills sharp.

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:43.870
Another cut scene of Nat training has her
punching a boxing bag, showing her relentless

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.989
determination to keep going.

00:00:45.989 --> 00:00:50.210
And in another cut scene of Nat sitting by
herself in the rain, we can see how lonely

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:51.250
she is.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:55.530
All these deleted scenes throw more light
on how Black Widow was really the only original

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.370
Avenger who refused to give up on the mission
over the five-year time jump.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:03.739
Although the Avengers hunt Thanos down on
his 'garden' planet and kill him, it doesn't

00:01:03.739 --> 00:01:08.570
reverse the snap and so, over the five years
that follow, Tony, Steve, Bruce, Clint and

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:13.770
Thor all go their own way with only Nat staying
on at Avengers HQ where she's determined to

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:18.480
keep the mission going, with surviving heroes
like Rocket, Okoye, Captain Marvel and War

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.290
Machine reporting in to her.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:23.820
It would have been nice to see these deleted
scenes to show what Nat was going through,

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:28.080
especially given how she reveals to Steve
and Clint that the Avengers were her one true

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.080
family.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.650
But I suspect they were likely cut for time,
as I can see they weren't absolutely essential

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.140
for the story.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.850
Another deleted scene for Black Widow comes
later during the time travel portion of the

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:40.690
movie when she and Hawkeye are on their way
to Vormir.

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:45.270
There's a clip cut from the final film where
Nat and Clint seem to be taking a moment before

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:49.650
they head on down to the Soul Stone planet
and it looks like this was probably some additional

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:52.490
foreshadowing of Nat's eventual fate.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:56.380
And a small moment from the first trailer
of Natasha looking on in shock at the carnage

00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:00.890
that Hawkeye has unleashed on the Yakuza in
Tokyo was also chopped from the final movie.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:05.810
We all know already from Avengers: Infinity
War that Marvel love to use fake and deleted

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:10.030
scenes in trailers to throw fans off the scent
when trying to figure out spoilers.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:14.050
And in Avengers: Endgame, Marvel have dialled
up the level of misdirection and trickery

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.050
to eleven.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:19.550
For example, in the final battle, during Captain
America's fight with Thanos, the Mad Titan

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:24.440
repeatedly brings down his huge double-bladed
sword on Cap's shield, smashing it several

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:26.910
times and leaving only part of it intact.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:31.569
But to avoid revealing this, in the trailers
when we see Cap dragging himself up from the

00:02:31.569 --> 00:02:35.350
ground, his shattered shield has been replaced
with an unbroken one.

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:39.240
In another shot from the battle, when Cap
tightens the shield strap on his arm as he

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:43.140
readies himself to face off against Thanos
again, in the movie, the shield is broken

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:46.910
at this point, but in the trailer we see it
still in one piece.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:51.880
In Infinity War, Bruce Banner wasn't able
to summon his inner Hulk successfully; but

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:56.850
in Endgame, during the 5-year time jump, Banner
finally comes to terms with the green guy

00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:01.760
and rather than trying to treat him as a disease,
he embraces him and becomes Professor Hulk,

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:04.330
getting what he calls the best of both worlds.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:08.950
To avoid this reveal before the movie was
released, Marvel digitally removed Hulk from

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.290
any scenes in the marketing materials.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:16.010
In this scene, where Rocket and Banner go
to New Asgard to find Thor, in the movie Professor

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:20.730
Hulk is actually right behind Rocket as the
racoon opens the door; but in the trailer,

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:22.870
he was digitally erased.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:26.880
And in this scene where War Machine meets
Ant-Man, in the movie, Professor Hulk walks

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:31.510
into the scene; but in the TV spot, the big
green guy was removed.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:36.000
Another major character change that Marvel
wanted to hide pre-release was Thor's transformation

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.950
from a bicep-busting hero to an overweight,
depressed God of Thunder, or what the Internet

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.390
is calling "Fat Thor".

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:46.590
Although Thor "went for the Mad Titan's head"
when they found him on the "garden" planet,

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:51.410
afterwards he fell into a deep depression,
abandoning his role as ruler of the Asgardians

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:55.750
and instead playing video games with Miek
and Korg while eating tons of junk food and

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:57.420
drowning his sorrows in beer.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:01.880
So, when Marvel presented us with shots of
Thor with his battle-ready Infinity War look

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.790
in the trailers, it was a complete misdirect.

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:09.459
For other Endgame trailer scenes, they completely
removed the Asgardian god so we wouldn't see

00:04:09.459 --> 00:04:10.980
the overweight Thor.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:15.450
In this scene of the Avengers figuring out
their Time Heist plan, both Thor and Professor

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.299
Hulk have been digitally erased from the shot.

00:04:18.299 --> 00:04:22.370
In a similar bit of trailer trickery, Thor
and Hulk were removed from this shot of the

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:26.509
team walking towards the time travel machine
at the Avengers Facility.

00:04:26.509 --> 00:04:31.169
Another attempt at misdirection is how Marvel
edited this shot of Thor to make it look more

00:04:31.169 --> 00:04:33.130
like he was somewhere like Wakanda.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:37.770
In the movie, this scene actually takes place
after Thor killed Thanos on his farm, but

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:41.699
in the trailer, the surrounding background
has been altered to give it a different look.

00:04:41.699 --> 00:04:46.270
There are some scenes teased in a TV spot
that were deleted from early in the movie

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:50.430
where Captain Marvel is with the team and
they're looking at screens of missing heroes.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:54.330
Carol, Steve and Rhodey are all wearing the
same clothes they had on in a scene which

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:58.940
was in the movie where Captain Marvel proposes
going to Thanos's 'garden' planet to take

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:00.370
the infinity stones back.

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:04.409
And there's also a similar deleted scene from
a trailer where Banner is looking at screens

00:05:04.409 --> 00:05:07.490
of Scott Lang, Shuri, and Peter Parker who
are missing.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:12.189
It's also strange that Endgame is missing
any mention of Nick Fury's pager from the

00:05:12.189 --> 00:05:13.990
Infinity War post-credits scene.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:17.710
Marvel kind of addressed this by releasing
the post-credits scene from Captain Marvel's

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.090
movie just before Endgame came out.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:26.819
"And tell me the second you get a signal,
I wanna know who's on the other end of that

00:05:26.819 --> 00:05:27.819
thing.

00:05:27.819 --> 00:05:29.120
Where's Fury?"

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:33.430
It's surprising this post-credits scene of
Carol meeting the team wasn't included in

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:37.680
Endgame with some additional footage of her
learning about the snap, because the Russo

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:42.099
Brothers have previously used post-credit
scenes from other Marvel movies in their own

00:05:42.099 --> 00:05:43.099
films.

00:05:43.099 --> 00:05:45.860
For example, the Bucky post-credits scene
from Ant-Man appeared in Captain America:

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.229
Civil War.

00:05:47.229 --> 00:05:51.150
Just before the Avengers split off into teams
to visit different timelines and retrieve

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:55.569
the Infinity Stones from the past, Cap gives
them all a pep talk and they put their hands

00:05:55.569 --> 00:05:57.120
together in a circle.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:00.809
For the trailers though, the time heist devices
that they're each wearing on their gloves

00:06:00.809 --> 00:06:02.009
have been removed.

00:06:02.009 --> 00:06:06.129
By the way, suitably enough, this shot is
an easter egg to a New Avengers comic book

00:06:06.129 --> 00:06:10.710
in which Marvel's Illuminati discuss the existence
of a multiverse and multiple parallel realities.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:16.430
And to avoid giving away more clues about
Endgame's time travel, in the trailers, Marvel

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:21.139
disguised the fact that this scene takes place
in 2012 during the Battle of New York.

00:06:21.139 --> 00:06:25.860
In the movie, Steve is wearing his blue Captain
America outfit from the first Avengers film,

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:28.780
and not his Infinity War costume we see here.

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.789
"You trust me?

00:06:30.789 --> 00:06:32.130
I do."

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:36.009
And the hand-shake between Tony and Steve
at the end of that clip was also cut from

00:06:36.009 --> 00:06:37.419
the final film.

00:06:37.419 --> 00:06:41.930
To avoid giving much away about the film's
third act, Marvel made a huge number of changes

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:45.930
to any scenes in the trailers taken from the
final battle against Thanos.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:50.899
In this scene of Iron Man, Cap and Thor walking
towards the Mad Titan, Thor's hammer Mjolnir

00:06:50.899 --> 00:06:52.270
has been erased.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:56.319
The existence of Mjolnir in Endgame, and how
Thor acquired it by going back in time to

00:06:56.319 --> 00:07:01.279
Asgard, needed to be kept secret as, before
Endgame, the hammer was last seen in Thor:

00:07:01.279 --> 00:07:03.849
Ragnarok where Hela destroyed it.

00:07:03.849 --> 00:07:08.499
This brief clip of Hawkeye fleeing down a
burning tunnel should actually show Outriders

00:07:08.499 --> 00:07:13.199
engulfed in the flames behind him, but to
avoid revealing that, Marvel scrubbed them

00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:14.689
out of the trailer.

00:07:14.689 --> 00:07:18.910
Clint was also carrying the new gauntlet with
the Infinity Stones at this point in the film,

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.949
another detail that was wiped out of the trailer.

00:07:21.949 --> 00:07:25.249
During this scene of Rocket and War Machine
assembling with Cap and the other heroes,

00:07:25.249 --> 00:07:31.050
in the movie, Giant-Man is rising up behind
them, except in the trailer he's been removed.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:35.310
Captain Marvel has a couple of new haircuts
in Endgame which Rocket makes a joke about

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:39.400
early on in the movie, but the short hairstyle
which Carol sports after the five-year time

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:42.979
jump in the film was replaced in the trailers
with Captain Marvel's helmet and mohawk as

00:07:42.979 --> 00:07:45.559
previously seen in her solo movie.

00:07:45.559 --> 00:07:55.330
And hair-related misdirections weren't limited
to Captain Marvel's role in Endgame.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:59.629
In this trailer clip where Nat sees Ant-Man
on the video camera arriving at the Avengers

00:07:59.629 --> 00:08:04.090
facility, she's still got her blond bob from
Infinity War, even though it happens five

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:05.179
years in the future.

00:08:05.179 --> 00:08:10.389
But, in the actual movie, at this point Natasha's
hair is long, loose, and mostly red mixed

00:08:10.389 --> 00:08:11.389
with some blond.

00:08:11.389 --> 00:08:15.599
By the way, Scott's line from the trailer
when he asks to be buzzed in was also deleted

00:08:15.599 --> 00:08:16.679
from the film.

00:08:16.679 --> 00:08:21.000
A character who never showed up in Endgame,
and who many fans missed, was Vision who Thanos

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.539
killed before the snap in Infinity War.

00:08:23.539 --> 00:08:28.310
Concept art of a ghostly grey-white Vision
leaked before Endgame suggesting we might

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:30.539
have seen the android return.

00:08:30.539 --> 00:08:34.820
Many fans had theorised Vision would return
in Endgame because when he was killed in Infinity

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:39.019
War he was drained of his colour, a possible
allusion to the transformation of his character

00:08:39.019 --> 00:08:41.919
in the comics after he was resurrected by
Hank Pym.

00:08:41.919 --> 00:08:46.440
But even though Vision didn't appear in Endgame,
he IS returning to the MCU with Scarlet Witch

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.649
in the not-too-distant future.

00:08:48.649 --> 00:08:53.040
Another technique Marvel used to try and prevent
secrets from leaking out was by giving actors

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:56.360
notorious for leaking spoilers only partial
scripts and then filming multiple endings.

00:08:56.360 --> 00:09:00.600
In an interview with E! News, Mark Ruffalo
revealed that he shot five different endings

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:01.600
for the movie.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:04.350
"I'm like shot five different endings to this
movie.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:07.490
I didn't even get a whole script to this movie.

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:08.959
I don't know why.

00:09:08.959 --> 00:09:12.810
The script I did get had... had dummy scenes
in it."

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:17.400
And I've got a separate video on that and
how despite all that Ruffalo still managed

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:21.791
to accidentally leak the actual ending of
Avengers Endgame many weeks before the film

00:09:21.791 --> 00:09:22.980
was released.

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:26.860
Tap in the top of the screen to check that
out or there's a link in the video description.

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:31.690
A cameo which appears to have been cut from
Endgame is by 13 Reasons Why star Katherine

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:35.790
Langford who was rumoured to be playing one
of two possible characters in the movie.

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:39.670
The first was Kate Bishop, one of the Young
Avengers in the comics who became Hawkeye

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:41.870
at a time when Clint wasn't around.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:47.250
Kate Bishop also worked with Clint for a while
after he returned, and if Langford did film

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:52.250
something, it's possible it was a teaser for
Hawkeye's upcoming TV series on Disney+, which

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:57.350
Variety says will show Clint passing the Hawkeye
mantle on to Kate Bishop.

00:09:57.350 --> 00:10:01.620
Before Endgame's release, another rumour was
that Langford would play Tony Stark's daughter

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:02.620
Morgan.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:06.491
This doesn't line up with the fact that Morgan
Stark was only 5 years old in Endgame, so

00:10:06.491 --> 00:10:11.150
that rumour seems unlikely unless she was
meant to appear to Tony as a vision of an

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:13.980
older Morgan in a flash-forward or dream.

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:17.410
When fans of the actress asked her on Instagram
what her character was supposed to be in Endgame,

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:19.250
she simply replied with a mysterious "…"

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:24.899
So, do you wish any of these deleted scenes
had been included in Avengers: Endgame?

00:10:24.899 --> 00:10:29.910
And what do you think about many of the scenes
in the trailers being faked or digitally edited?

